  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowerment and Development for Girls&apos; Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve access, participation and educational outcomes for girls in the Zambia government school system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Senior officials, policy makers and school leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EDGE programme seeks to improved access, equity, safeguarding and better educational outcomes for girls in the Zambian national education system. It does this by delivering a range of interventions and products including: consultancy and support for the senior leadership of the Ministry of Education on strategy and policy in relation to girls&apos; education supported by research and insight pieces, policy briefs, capacity development for senior management in framing and operationalising strategy, support for the Ministry on strategic communication, development of data gathering capacity to support evidence based decision making.</narrative>
  </description>
